00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.040
Doesn't he? I mean, he starts out a little slower.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.220
I mean, maybe it's a little smoother of a transition.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.340
Yeah, that is basically like the definition of building momentum.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.160
Right. I think he's sticky though.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:12.340
He's got sticky shoes.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:24.280
I think the difference between momentum between someone like Mylon and the way that Mario works in, say, Super Mario Brothers 3 with the P meter is that that meter is gradual.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:32.700
And actually, like the way that it happens isn't that you start off with like no weight and room to jump around and stuff like that.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:35.140
It's that it's a gradual climb.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:41.320
